<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.67 bln on Feb 28.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.67 bln on Feb 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.67 billion on February 28, 1997 from $23.48 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Feb 28	Feb 21	 Mar 1</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,695	19,374	 15,912</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,977	 4,097	  4,659</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	    11	     49</p>
<p>    Total			     23,674	23,482	 20,620</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
